    "subject_name": "Physics",
    "chapter_id": "6160241f1a832a8dea12fbf0",
    "chapter_name": "Magnetic Effects of Current",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_2"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The electric current in a circular coil of four turns produces a magnetic induction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> at its centre. The coil is unwound and is rewound into a circular coil of single turn, the magnetic induction at the centre of the coil by the same current will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Magnetic field at the centre of the coil is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now in the first case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>and for the second case:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>As the length of the wire will remain same, therefore</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Hence, required ratio will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math></p>"
  }
}